WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.544 --> 00:00:03.545
Announcer: Three...

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:05.255
Announcer: Two...

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:06.715
Announcer: One...

00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:08.383
Announcer: Blast off!

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:10.301
Announcer: To a new beginning

00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:11.720
Announcer: beyond the stars.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.471
America's famous for

00:00:13.471 --> 00:00:14.931
the notion that

00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:16.099
it's the land of opportunity.

00:00:16.641 --> 00:00:17.934
Americans promising 

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.060
more than we can deliver. 

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.603
That's the center 
of Hello Tomorrow. 

00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:23.398
Announcer: Start living your brighter tomorrow

00:00:23.398 --> 00:00:23.940
Announcer: today!

00:00:24.482 --> 00:00:26.693
The show is about 
the American dream

00:00:28.403 --> 00:00:29.904
and how askew it can go. 

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:33.158
This show is so unique.

00:00:33.158 --> 00:00:34.409
I have a hard time describing it. 

00:00:35.493 --> 00:00:36.703
Hello Tomorrow is about

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.204
a bunch of salesmen.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.914
      They're selling timeshares

00:00:39.914 --> 00:00:41.666
for a property on the moon

00:00:41.666 --> 00:00:42.834
called the Brightside.

00:00:43.668 --> 00:00:45.545
It's a futuristic 

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.338
story told in a retro way.

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:50.759
Automatically I was interested.

00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:55.054
You're introduced to this world

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:56.931
through Jack Billings.

00:00:56.931 --> 00:00:58.016
He's got a sales team

00:00:58.016 --> 00:01:00.477
of misfits and vagabonds. 

00:01:00.477 --> 00:01:03.480
Shirley absolutely runs this business. 

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.481
Incredibly shrewd,

00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:05.440
very capable,

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.025
perfect counterpart to Jack. 

00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:08.359
They're giving people

00:01:08.359 --> 00:01:10.361
an opportunity to hope
 for a better future. 

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.864
The Brightside.

00:01:12.864 --> 00:01:14.199
That's a place for real people. 

00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:15.158
To start fresh,

00:01:15.158 --> 00:01:16.534
unwind, retire. 

00:01:17.952 --> 00:01:19.704
It is 1950's retro future. 

00:01:20.455 --> 00:01:22.707
The sets, cars, clothing. 

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.751
There's something so fun

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.503
about imagining a world that's

00:01:26.503 --> 00:01:28.046
never been seen before. 

00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:31.633
We built a lot of the robots practically. 

00:01:33.051 --> 00:01:34.177
You've got puppeteers.

00:01:34.177 --> 00:01:35.261
Remote control.

00:01:36.012 --> 00:01:37.222
They make a lot of noise. 

00:01:37.222 --> 00:01:40.141
I have so many emotional scenes,

00:01:40.141 --> 00:01:41.851
where in the background

00:01:41.851 --> 00:01:43.394
is this little one eyed tin can

00:01:43.394 --> 00:01:44.979
Zizz. Zizz.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:47.857
The beginning of the show

00:01:47.857 --> 00:01:50.527
is defined by such optimism. 

00:01:50.693 --> 00:01:52.195
I'm out delivering smiles.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:53.655
[ SMASH ]

00:01:53.822 --> 00:01:55.365
And then very quickly

00:01:55.365 --> 00:01:56.616
it is made clear

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:59.035
there is a lot more 
ominous undertones.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.495
It's kind of funny

00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:02.038
how good things can be 

00:02:02.038 --> 00:02:04.123
without the truth getting in the way. 

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:05.333
And action!

00:02:06.751 --> 00:02:08.294
I found it incredibly

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.838
entertaining to imagine a world

00:02:09.838 --> 00:02:11.172
that's talking about 

00:02:11.172 --> 00:02:12.882
the spirit of American salesmanship. 

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.343
Jack, compulsively,

00:02:15.343 --> 00:02:16.803
seeks happiness

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:19.013
and to satisfy anyone in front of him. 

00:02:20.515 --> 00:02:22.308
That sense of hopefulness as

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.435
lie upon lie begins 
to crumble down

00:02:26.187 --> 00:02:27.438
I've never seen

00:02:27.438 --> 00:02:28.773
it put on page before. 

00:02:30.233 --> 00:02:32.402
We rely on storytelling

00:02:32.402 --> 00:02:34.028
to make sense of our world. 

00:02:34.737 --> 00:02:36.155
In this alternative future

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:37.407
nothing is any different. 

00:02:37.407 --> 00:02:39.617
All the gadgets break. 
At a certain point, 

00:02:39.617 --> 00:02:41.119
your bartender robot might 

00:02:41.119 --> 00:02:42.912
be able to serve you a
 beer from its belly, 

00:02:42.912 --> 00:02:45.039
but there might be a little
bit of motor oil in it. 

00:02:46.291 --> 00:02:47.500
Hey there, fella. 

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.002
My eyes are up here. 

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.712
We promise perfection

00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:52.255
and what we deliver is human. 

00:02:54.716 --> 00:02:56.175
I'm excited for audiences

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:58.261
to see the chemistry on set. 

00:02:59.262 --> 00:02:59.721
That can't be on there. 

00:03:00.138 --> 00:03:01.723
We do a lot of laughing

00:03:01.723 --> 00:03:03.892
but it's quite emotional 
at the same time. 

00:03:03.892 --> 00:03:06.644
I will burn this whole 
place to the ground. 

00:03:08.146 --> 00:03:09.856
This is about what we
 still all wrestle with.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.190
What's the truth?

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.066
What's a lie?

00:03:12.066 --> 00:03:13.568
What do I actually believe in?

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.112
It is funny,

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.157
and thoughtful,

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:22.035
and odd.

00:03:22.911 --> 00:03:24.746
But everybody in their own way

00:03:24.746 --> 00:03:27.165
is trying to be a better human. 

